  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Assuming "forensic science" means one job: the lab-coat crime-scene investigator',
    body: "That single image covers maybe two of the eight tracks above. Digital forensics and forensic accounting run through completely different degrees, employers, and pay scales, and most people never hear about them until well after choosing a college.",
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Treating forensic psychology or profiling as a mainstream career path based on television and true-crime media',
    body: 'The real Indian job market for this specific specialisation is thin. Anyone drawn to this track specifically should verify current opening counts with a working forensic psychologist before committing years of study to it.',
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    title: 'Ignoring the digital forensics track because it "sounds like IT, not forensic science"',
    body: "It is, by employer count and by pay ceiling, the fastest-growing track on this entire list right now, and it is open to a CS/IT background plus the right certification, not only to forensic science graduates.",
