    q: 'How is BNSS changing demand for forensic science careers?',
    a: 'The Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, which replaced the CrPC, made forensic evidence collection mandatory at the crime scene for offences carrying a sentence of seven years or more. That is a legal requirement, not a hiring trend that could quietly reverse, and it is a direct driver of new recruitment across state Forensic Science Laboratories on top of the pre-existing shortage in trained forensic staff.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Should I read the "is forensic science a good career" verdict article too?',
    a: "Yes, if you are still deciding whether forensic science is worth pursuing at all. Read is forensic science a good career in India for the honest pay, competition, and AI-risk verdict. This article assumes you are past that question and answers the next one: once you commit to forensic science, which of the eight real tracks should you actually aim for.",
